{"format":"tvf-scene","v":1,"name":"example · Holding in order","loop":56,"ease":"inout","hold":0,"gravity":1,"wind":0,"trail":null,"camera":[{"t":0,"box":[-0.815288889,-0.103895551,-0.611377778,0.08542889]},{"t":0.16,"box":[-0.815288889,-0.103895551,-0.611377778,0.08542889]},{"t":0.19,"box":[-0.517422222,-0.0663111111,-0.358133333,0.0863111111]},{"t":0.33,"box":[-0.517422222,-0.0663111111,-0.358133333,0.0863111111]},{"t":0.36,"box":[-0.230577778,-0.0745777778,-0.0294222222,0.0705777778]},{"t":0.5,"box":[-0.230577778,-0.0745777778,-0.0294222222,0.0705777778]},{"t":0.53,"box":[0.0550666667,-0.0693777778,0.262711111,0.0427111111]},{"t":0.67,"box":[0.0550666667,-0.0693777778,0.262711111,0.0427111111]},{"t":0.7,"box":[0.3472,-0.0781333333,0.548355556,0.0750222222]},{"t":0.84,"box":[0.3472,-0.0781333333,0.548355556,0.0750222222]},{"t":0.87,"box":[0.636088889,-0.0816888889,0.837244444,0.0750222222]}],"stops":[0.16,0.33,0.5,0.67,0.84],"beats":[{"title":"A stream through an unknown gain","text":"A screen receives [a stream of amounts](#lit:1), each multiplied somewhere along the way by a gain no one recorded. Scale the world: double the gain, and every arrival moves, and so does every difference of two.\n\n[Each arrival over the last](#lit:4) does not move. That is a reading. [The first arrival](#lit:2), alone, says nothing: it founds what the reader will hold, and that is all."},{"title":"One slot","text":"To read an arrival against something, the reader must already hold something: the hold. Each look states one reading, the direction [hold : arrival], [a ray from home](#lit:9) that crosses [a post one hold out](#lit:7) at arrival ÷ hold.\n\n[The corner](#lit:11), 1, means nothing changed. The register names each reading by [a whole number of steps](#lit:12) of one ratio, here 1.25. With an odd number of steps one is centred on the corner, and a still scene reads still; with an even number the corner is a boundary, and the essay's 32-step register returns the hold × 1.01815 on every look of a scene that is not moving."},{"title":"Reading is seeking","text":"The unit rule: hold the arrival that filled you, until the next one says otherwise. [The hold](#lit:16) stays while [the stream](#lit:15) reads within [one step either side](#lit:14), and [moves to the arrival](#lit:17) when it leaves. Here it held 67 looks and moved 13.\n\nWhat the moves buy is not accuracy but stretches of agreement: at a move the reading is exactly 1, and one statement holds until the stream contradicts it. On the essay's random walk the rule held 1,622 times in 2,000 and moved 378; a predicting rule moves every look, and its reading changes sign at 67% of looks against the unit rule's 31%."},{"title":"The side bit","text":"An arrival above the hold or below it is one bit. Step [the hold](#lit:22) toward whichever side keeps winning, and it settles on the arrivals' [median](#lit:20): Robbins and Monro's sign rule. Here 2,000 arrivals of a stream with median 10 and no mean, read on a log axis: the hold from 2 to near 10, [the running mean](#lit:21) wandering past 40.\n\nThe median commutes with every increasing change of what arrives; the mean does not. On the essay's stream the hold settled at 9.25 while the mean wandered to 16.09."},{"title":"Where each rule's corner falls","text":"Every rule holds something, so every rule has a look where the arrival meets what it holds. The unit rule holds the last arrival: its corners are where [the tide](#lit:24) stops rising and starts falling, [its highs and lows](#lit:25).\n\nA trend rule holds a forecast, the last arrival plus the last change. Its corners say the forecast came true, and they fall [on the straight stretches](#lit:26), the inflections. Across missing looks the essay's races found the unit rule's turns 3.01% off with half the looks gone, the trend's 60.58%: a carry that extrapolates is most wrong exactly at a turn."},{"title":"Order alone","text":"[The same tide](#lit:28) in metres, then in feet from another datum, then cubed: the amounts move every time. [The turns](#lit:29) do not. A turn is a sign of the reading changing, and no strictly increasing change of what arrives can move a sign.\n\nRead every third look, [the turns](#lit:30) come out within two received looks of their own. On NOAA's recorded tides at Boston and San Francisco the split held exactly: order alone kept every turn under a new datum, feet and a cube. The tide here is two sines made for the picture. [The essay](https://github.com/reportbase/wander/blob/main/papers/essays/11-holding-in-order.md)"}],"path":null,"items":[{"fill":{"color":"#f4f1ea","opacity":1},"stroke":null,"width":0,"open":false,"exact":{"x":[-0.9,0.9,0.9,-0.9],"y":[0.211111111,0.211111111,-0.211111111,-0.211111111],"r":null,"smooth":null,"ctrl":null,"holes":[]}},{"morph":1},{"morph":2},{"morph":0},{"morph":3},{"morph":4},{"morph":5},{"morph":7},{"morph":8},{"morph":12},{"morph":9},{"morph":10},{"morph":11},{"morph":6},{"morph":14},{"morph":13},{"morph":15},{"morph":16},{"morph":17},{"morph":18},{"morph":19},{"morph":20},{"morph":21},{"morph":22},{"morph":23},{"morph":24},{"morph":25},{"morph":26},{"morph":27},{"morph":28},{"morph":29},{"morph":30},{"morph":31},{"morph":33},{"morph":34},{"morph":35},{"morph":32},{"morph":36},{"morph":37},{"morph":38},{"morph":39},{"morph":40},{"morph":41},{"morph":42}],"morphs":[{"exact":true,"open":true,"holes":null,"keys":[{"x":[-0.795555556,-0.631111111],"y":[-0.02,-0.02],"r":[0,0],"c":[null,null]}],"fill":null,"inPlace":true,"lag":0,"fx":null,"own":{"parent":-1,"parentAt":null,"follow":null,"look":-1,"lookRef":0,"phase":0,"rate":1,"spin":0,"motion":null,"onto":null,"laps":1,"start":null,"times":null,"clip":{"start":0.004,"len":0.986,"show":"","in":{"kind":"draw","len":0.01}},"eases":null,"straight":false,"trail":null,"cols":null,"path":null},"stroke":"#3b4256","width":2,"strokeOpacity":1},{"exact":true,"open":false,"holes":null,"keys":[{"x":[-0.783111111,-0.783111111,-0.776444444,-0.77644444